 "reading": "Across the nine fin genes, 11 alignment columns show a residue shared by gliders of two or more lineages and absent from their non-gliding relatives, against 17 columns for the role-swapped baseline. At the lat4a site where flying fishes and gliding halfbeaks carry L, every other glider and flier with data carries F: the fish convergence does not extend to mammals. Gliders do not resemble each other more than they resemble other lineages' non-gliders (see mean_identity_cross_lineage): identity follows ancestry, not gliding. Most of the few 'convergent' columns pair colugos with bats, two lineages whose control is the same human sequence, so a human-specific residue alone produces them; they are not evidence of shared glider biology."
